  "name": "Butyrate biosynthesis (butyryl-CoA pathway)",
  "description": "The butyryl-CoA pathway is the predominant route for butyrate production in Firmicutes. Acetyl-CoA is condensed and reduced through acetoacetyl-CoA, 3-hydroxybutyryl-CoA, crotonyl-CoA and butyryl-CoA, finally yielding butyrate via butyrate kinase or phosphate butyryltransferase / butyrate kinase (Buk). It operates in cross-feeding with acetate producers that supply acetyl-CoA precursors.",
